Attribution required from downstream users
------------------------------------------

When reusing this dataset, retain the following notice:

  Contains information from EUR-Lex, © European Union, 1998-2026,
  licensed under CC BY 4.0. Structured, identified and diffed by
  EUCITE. Modified from the original.

Every node in the dataset names the source work (by its CELEX identifier) and
the language it was read from. The manifest that accompanies the dataset gives,
for each source, its URL, the time it was retrieved and its checksums, so
attribution can be reconstructed per node rather than only per dataset.


Indication of modifications
---------------------------

CC BY 4.0 requires that changes be indicated. This project makes the following
modifications to the upstream material:

  - the text is segmented into a typed node tree, and each node carries the
    text of everything it contains;
  - identifiers are attached to each node — inherited from the source where the
    source provides them, derived by this project's parser below the paragraph
    level (each node declares which of the two applies);
  - whitespace is normalised and presentation markup is removed; footnotes are
    moved to a separate field; superscripts are written with a caret (10^25);
    numbers marked as such are grouped by thousands, as the Official Journal
    prints them;
  - amendment markers are extracted into structured fields, and provisions that
    the consolidated text marks as deleted are kept as identifiers without
    text;
  - the formulae of the preamble and the final part (place, date, signatures)
    are not included;
  - several source works are distributed together, one file per work and
    language.

Apart from these, no word of the provisions included is altered, added or
removed.


